Evaluator: A. Psaltis (04/2025)
Comments:
1. Resonances at Er= 798 and 880 keV: their strengths were taken by Best et al. (2013) with a 20% and 50% uncertainty.
The data from Denker, Ph.D. thesis (1994) were excluded because of large background contribution from the 13C(α,n)16O reaction.
See the discussion at Best et al. (2013).
2. Spin/parities for are adopted from the R-matrix fit of Best et al. (2013) for resonances with Er>900 keV. In the case of discrepancies between
the valeus of Best et al. and NNDC, we normalized the G_a so that omega*G_a=constant. A 50% mixing is assumed.
3. For the calculation of G_n, we have added the partial neutron widths (G_n0+G_n1) reported in Best et al. (2013).
4. We assigned 10 keV energy uncertainty to 1506 and 1657 keV resonances, due to no report at NNDC.
5. S-factor at high energies taken from Hansen et al. (1967) with a factor of 5 and 2 uncertainty for E below and above 10 MeV, respectively.
